@startuml
title CMTAT RuleEngine — transfer validation dispatch
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false

actor "Token holder" as H
participant "CMTAT\n(or ERC-3643 token)" as T
participant "RuleEngine" as RE
participant "Rule 0\n(e.g. Whitelist)" as R0
participant "Rule 1" as R1
participant "Rule n" as Rn

H -> T : 1. transfer(to, value)
T -> RE : 2. transferred(from, to, value)
note right of T
  ERC-3643 transfer hook.
  CMTAT v3.3.0+ also passes the spender/operator
  (spender-aware path) so mint/burn/transferFrom
  operators are visible to the rules.
end note
RE -> R0 : 3a. transferred(...)
RE -> R1 : 3b. transferred(...)
RE -> Rn : 3c. transferred(...)
note over RE, Rn
  The RuleEngine forwards the check to every configured rule;
  any rule that reverts blocks the transfer.
end note

note over T, RE
  Each Rule itself implements the RuleEngine interface, so a single Rule
  can be set **directly** on CMTAT as its rule engine (no RuleEngine controller).
  Use the RuleEngine only when several rules must be combined on one token.
end note
@enduml
